Needs:
* Node v14.6.0 >=
* (optional) typescript 3.8.3 (future versions add unwanted transpiled code)
  npm install -g typescript@3.8.3

To try:
Open index.html in a browser.

To run a file:
node jsetimos.js fileName

To run in shell mode (REPL):
node jsetimos.js

To run from raw input (untested):
node jsetimos.js --inputMode "print("hello")"

Import files:
    Base dir is main file running directory.
    JSEtimos file extension is *.jk

Optional: If you made some changes on the jsetimos.ts file you will need to recompile again to js.
Needs the node type definitions next to it (npm install @types/node@14) and must use -p:
the source has known type errors, so "tsc -b" refuses to write the output.
tsc -p .

Go implementation (src/go, needs Go 1.21 or newer):
./build_go.sh           builds ./jsetimos (jsetimos.exe on Windows)
./build_go.sh --test    builds and runs the unit and bug regression tests

Bug regression tests (see BUGS_AUDIT.MD):
tests/bugs/run.sh [node|go|both]

If you want some syntax highlight when editing 
jsetimos code you can use the kotlin highlighter
of your editor of choice, will work well enough.

